🛠️ CAD & Mechanical Design

The Robodog is being developed using 3D CAD modeling to design and refine the complete quadruped mechanical structure before fabrication.

The CAD model includes:

🐕 Complete quadruped body assembly
🦿 Four-leg mechanical structure
⚙️ Leg joints and servo mounting mechanisms
🔩 Servo brackets and mechanical linkages
🧩 Modular body and leg components
📐 Dimensional and assembly constraints
⚖️ Weight and mass distribution analysis
🔧 Design for manufacturing and assembly
🖨️ Components suitable for 3D printing / fabrication
🔄 Iterative mechanical design and prototyping
📐 CAD Development Workflow
Concept Design
      ↓
3D CAD Modelling
      ↓
Individual Part Design
      ↓
Assembly
      ↓
Motion & Interference Checking
      ↓
Weight / Mass Analysis
      ↓
Design Optimization
      ↓
Prototype / Fabrication
      ↓
Testing & Iteration
🧱 Modular Design

The mechanical structure follows a modular approach, allowing individual components such as legs, brackets, joints, and body sections to be modified or replaced without redesigning the complete robot.

This makes the platform easier to:

Maintain
Repair
Upgrade
Manufacture
Experiment with different leg configurations
